    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "ARRAYS\n\nAn array is an ordered list of values of one type. Generic array nodes (Length, Contains, Slice ...)\nlearn their element type from the wire they are connected to, so an array needs a typed source:\nhere String Split makes [pear, apple, fig, kiwi]. Array nodes never change an array in place: Slice\nRETURNS a new, shorter array, which is wired onward. Length, Contains and Is Empty answer questions\nabout whichever array you wire into them.\nClass variables hold single values (numbers, text, booleans), so the collection itself lives on the wires between nodes and only the answers are stored in variables.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          250.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "SOURCE\nString Split makes the array [pear, apple, fig, kiwi]. Its element type (String) flows down the wire to every array node.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          460.0
        ],
        "size": [
          330.0,
          110.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "src"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "QUESTIONS\nArray Length (4), Array Contains \"fig\" (true) and Array Is Empty (false) all read the same array wire; each answer is stored in a variable by a Set node.",
        "position": [
          360.0,
          720.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          110.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.9,
          0.55,
          0.15,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "len",
          "has",
          "empty"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-4",
        "text": "SLICE AND JOIN\nArray Slice (start 1, end 3) returns a NEW array [apple, fig]; String Join turns it into \"apple,fig\". The original array is untouched.",
        "position": [
          1260.0,
